.TH mbedit-qt 1 "2 November 2026" "MB-System 5.0" "MB-System 5.0"
.SH NAME
\fBmbedit-qt\fP \- Interactive editor used to flag bad bathymetry values in swath sonar bathymetry data (Qt6 version).

.SH VERSION
Version 5.0

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmbedit-qt\fP
.br
[--begin-time=yr/mo/da/hr/mn/sc {-Byr/mo/da/hr/mn/sc}
.br
--browse {-D}
.br
--end-time=yr/mo/da/hr/mn/sc {-Eyr/mo/da/hr/mn/sc}
.br
--format=format_id {-Fformat_id}
.br
--gui-mode {-G}
.br
--help {-H}
.br
--input=file {-Ifile}
.br
--reference=grid
.br
--run-mbprocess {-X}
.br
--use-edit-save {-S}
.br
--verbose {-V}
.br
--dump
.br
--export=image [--size=WxH]
.br
--replay=script]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmbedit-qt\fP is a Qt6 port of \fBmbedit\fP. It displays the bathymetry
profiles of several pings and lets the user flag and unflag soundings. The
edits are written to an edit save file, which \fBmbprocess\fP applies when it
writes a processed swath file. It reads and writes the same edit save
files, parameter files and lock files as \fBmbedit\fP, so a file can move
between the two programs. The two cannot edit one file at the same time.

The window can be resized, and it follows the light or dark mode of the system.

